All 15 tests pass. Here's a summary of the 10 bugs fixed across 3 files:

**`src/auth.py`** (3 test fixes)
- `has_permission`: compared roles case-sensitively — now lowercases both sides
- `is_admin_or_owner`: used `and` instead of `or` — now correctly checks admin **or** owner

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 test fixes)
- Mutable default `{}` shared state across instances — changed to `None` default, creates a new dict per instance
- `add` overwrote quantities instead of accumulating — now uses `+=`
- `reserve` used `>=` instead of `>` — reserving exactly the available stock is now allowed
- `release` allowed reserved count to go negative — now raises `ValueError` when releasing more than reserved

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 test fixes)
- `slugify` didn't lowercase characters — now lowercases each alphanumeric char
- `slugify`'s single-pass `replace("--", "-")` didn't fully collapse runs of dashes — switched to `re.sub(r"-+", "-", ...)`
- `truncate` appended the suffix beyond `max_len` — now truncates to `max_len - len(suffix)` before adding the suffix
